{%- comment -%}
  sections/banner.liquid — the Gift Guide hero (Figma frame 1:1589).

  Built from scratch: no Dawn section, snippet, component or CSS class is used
  anywhere in this file (C1). The only snippets rendered are our own, `ee-`
  prefixed ones.

  Three stacked bands, matching the design (docs/DESIGN-TOKENS.md §1):
    1. a utility bar carrying the wordmark, the merchant's message and the CTA
       (the message and the CTA are desktop-only — the mobile frame `1:1804`
       shows the wordmark and a hamburger and nothing else)
    2. the hero: full-bleed illustration, heading, description, animated button
    3. the announcement strip

  This section owns all seven of the instruction page's red rectangles, and
  every one of them is a schema setting (C5, ADR-011):
    1 wordmark          → logo + logo_alt
    2 top-bar message   → utility_text
    3 top-bar CTA       → utility_cta_label + utility_cta_url
    4 H1                → heading
    5 description       → description
    6 SHOP NOW button   → button_label + button_url
    7 bottom strip      → strip_text
  Each is guarded so the section still renders when the merchant leaves it
  empty. Items 2 and 3 are hidden below 768 — that is visibility only; they
  stay settings at every width.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'ee-tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'ee-button.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'ee-banner.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  # Jost ships in Shopify's own font library, so it loads through font_picker +
  # font_face rather than a Google Fonts <link>, which would be an external
  # runtime dependency (C2, DESIGN-TOKENS §4.3).
  assign ee_font_body = section.settings.font_body
  assign ee_font_heading = ee_font_body | font_modify: 'weight', '500'
  unless ee_font_heading
    # Not every family in the library carries a 500; fall back to the regular
    # face rather than emitting a broken @font-face rule.
    assign ee_font_heading = ee_font_body
  endunless

  # The illustration is decorative: it carries no information the heading does
  # not already carry. Defaulting its alt to the heading made a screen reader
  # announce "The Gift Guide" twice in a row (S7.4), so the hero gets its own
  # setting instead, empty by default — the correct markup for a decorative
  # image. A merchant who uploads a *meaningful* illustration can fill it in,
  # and an uploaded file's own alt still wins over an empty setting.
  assign ee_hero_alt = section.settings.image_alt

  # The wordmark carries its own alt, because it is artwork with no text behind
  # it (ADR-011) and neither an uploaded file's alt nor any other setting says
  # what it reads.
  assign ee_logo_alt = section.settings.logo_alt
-%}

{%- style -%}
  {{ ee_font_body | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}
  {{ ee_font_heading | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}

  /* Per-instance only: two sections on one page can carry different fonts.
     The selector deliberately includes the section id AND the block class:
     ee-tokens.css declares the fallback families on `.ee-scope`, which is this
     same element, so an inherited value from the wrapper alone would lose. */
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .ee-banner {
    --ee-font-body: {{ ee_font_body.family }}, {{ ee_font_body.fallback_families }};
    --ee-banner-heading-weight: {{ ee_font_heading.weight }};
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div class="ee-scope ee-banner" data-ee-banner>
  {%- comment -%} Band 1 — utility bar: red rectangles 1, 2 and 3. {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="ee-banner__utility">
    <div class="ee-banner__utility-row">
      {%- comment -%}
        Red rectangle #1 — the TISSO VISON wordmark. `1:1591` is a GROUP of
        nine VECTOR paths, not a TEXT node: it is outlined artwork with no font
        behind it, so it cannot be a text setting. Per ADR-011 it is an
        image_picker plus its own alt string, falling back to artwork we ship
        in assets/ when the merchant has uploaded nothing.

        The fallback is a plain <img>: if `ee-wordmark.svg` is not present the
        browser renders the alt text instead. It degrades, it does not error.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ee-banner__brand">
        {%- if section.settings.logo != blank -%}
          {%- render 'ee-image',
            image: section.settings.logo,
            class: 'ee-banner__logo',
            widths: '160,240,320,480',
            sizes: '152px',
            alt: ee_logo_alt,
            loading: 'eager'
          -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <img
            class="ee-banner__logo"
            src="{{ 'ee-wordmark.svg' | asset_url }}"
            width="152"
            height="19"
            alt="{{ ee_logo_alt | escape }}"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Red rectangle #2. Hidden below 768 by CSS, never by Liquid. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.utility_text != blank -%}
        <p class="ee-banner__utility-message">{{ section.settings.utility_text | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Red rectangle #3. The same ee-button snippet as the hero's SHOP NOW,
        so both carry the identical two-state animation (Figma "Component 207";
        `1:1605` and `43:377` are instances of the same component).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'ee-button',
        label: section.settings.utility_cta_label,
        url: section.settings.utility_cta_url,
        variant: 'accent',
        fill: true,
        class: 'ee-banner__cta'
      -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Band 2 — hero.

    <section>, not <div>, and <header> for the copy block below — and that is a
    correctness fix, not a stylistic one. Dawn's `assets/base.css:483-495`
    declares `a:empty, ul:empty, dl:empty, div:empty, section:empty,
    article:empty, p:empty, h1:empty … { display: none }`. With the heading,
    description and button all blank the copy block became `:empty`, Dawn hid
    it, and the hero — whose height comes entirely from that block, since the
    illustration is absolutely positioned — collapsed to 0px, taking the
    merchant's uploaded image with it.

    `<header>` is not in Dawn's list, so the rule simply does not match; no
    override, no `!important`, no fight with the host theme. `<section>` IS in
    the list, but this band always contains the illustration <img>, so it can
    never be `:empty` — and wrapping the <header> in sectioning content is what
    keeps it a generic element instead of a second `banner` landmark competing
    with Dawn's real page header.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section class="ee-banner__hero">
    {%- comment -%}
      The design's line-art illustration is 78 vector paths across two groups
      (`8593:227`). S2.3 requires it to be a merchant-supplied image_picker, so
      it ships as a single full-bleed background image. It is above the fold:
      eager, and flagged high priority so it does not queue behind the grid.

      The artwork does not exist in the store's catalogue, so — same pattern as
      the wordmark — we ship it in assets/ and the picker only overrides it.
      That way the hero is never blank. If `ee-banner-art.png` is absent the
      <img> falls back to its alt text rather than erroring.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
      {%- render 'ee-image',
        image: section.settings.image,
        class: 'ee-banner__image',
        widths: '375,550,750,1100,1440,1920,2400',
        sizes: '100vw',
        alt: ee_hero_alt,
        loading: 'eager',
        fetchpriority: 'high'
      -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <img
        class="ee-banner__image"
        src="{{ 'ee-banner-art.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="2880"
        height="1560"
        alt="{{ ee_hero_alt | escape }}"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    {%- endif -%}

    <header class="ee-banner__content">
      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          <h1>: on a page template Dawn's header renders the shop name as a
          <div>, so this is the page's first heading and the grid's <h2> follows
          it without skipping a level (S7.6).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="ee-banner__heading">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.description != blank -%}
        <div class="ee-banner__description">{{ section.settings.description }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        `fill: true` because `3:1672` is a FIXED 119px label cell with
        `textAlignHorizontal: CENTER` inside the 193px mobile button — the
        slack sits inside the label, not between the label and the arrow.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- render 'ee-button',
        label: section.settings.button_label,
        url: section.settings.button_url,
        variant: 'dark',
        fill: true,
        class: 'ee-banner__button'
      -%}
    </header>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Band 3 — announcement strip, red rectangle #7.

    Two strings, not one, because the design has two. `1:1613.characters` is
    "SUSTAINABLE, ETHICALLY MADE CLOTHES IN SIZES XXS TO 6XL" (55 chars at 16px,
    box 451 × 14); `1:1813.characters` is "SUSTAINABLE, ETHICALLY MADE
    ACTIVEWEAR" (38 chars at 14px, box 288 × 14). Serving the desktop string at
    375 is what inflated the band from the designed 34px to 46.84 — at 14px it
    measures ≈394px of ink against 342px of content width, so it wraps to two
    lines. No CSS can fix that; only the shorter copy the design actually
    specifies can. This settles the ASSUMPTION flagged in DESIGN-TOKENS §7.1.

    Both are schema settings (C5) and each falls back to the other, so a
    merchant who fills in only one still gets a strip at every width. The hidden
    variant is `display: none`, which removes it from the accessibility tree too
    — a screen reader reads the strip once, not twice.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign ee_strip_wide = section.settings.strip_text | default: section.settings.strip_text_mobile
    assign ee_strip_narrow = section.settings.strip_text_mobile | default: section.settings.strip_text
  -%}
  {%- if ee_strip_wide != blank -%}
    <div class="ee-banner__strip">
      <p class="ee-banner__strip-text ee-banner__strip-text--narrow">{{ ee_strip_narrow | escape }}</p>
      <p class="ee-banner__strip-text ee-banner__strip-text--wide">{{ ee_strip_wide | escape }}</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "EE Banner",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Wordmark"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "logo",
      "label": "Wordmark image",
      "info": "The design's wordmark is outlined artwork, not type, so it is an image. Leave empty to use the artwork bundled with the theme."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "logo_alt",
      "label": "Wordmark alt text",
      "default": "Tisso Vison",
      "info": "Read out by screen readers, and shown if the image cannot load."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Utility bar"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The message and the button appear from 768px up. The mobile design shows only the wordmark in this bar."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "utility_text",
      "label": "Message",
      "default": "Find the ideal gift for your loved ones."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "utility_cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "choose gift"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "utility_cta_url",
      "label": "Button link"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Hero"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Background illustration",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the line-art illustration bundled with the theme."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "image_alt",
      "label": "Illustration alt text",
      "info": "Leave empty: the illustration is decorative and the heading beside it already carries the meaning. Fill this in only if your artwork says something the heading does not."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "The Gift Guide"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Description",
      "default": "<p>Discover Joy: Your Ultimate Holiday Gift Destination. Explore our curated selection and find the perfect gifts to delight your loved ones this holiday season.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "Shop Now"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "button_url",
      "label": "Button link"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Announcement strip"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "strip_text",
      "label": "Text (768px and up)",
      "default": "SUSTAINABLE, ETHICALLY MADE CLOTHES IN SIZES XXS TO 6XL"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "strip_text_mobile",
      "label": "Text (below 768px)",
      "default": "SUSTAINABLE, ETHICALLY MADE ACTIVEWEAR",
      "info": "The design uses a shorter line on mobile so the strip stays one line tall. Leave empty to reuse the wider text."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Typography"
    },
    {
      "type": "font_picker",
      "id": "font_body",
      "label": "Banner font",
      "default": "jost_n4",
      "info": "The design uses Jost. Loaded from Shopify's font library, not from an external CDN."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "EE Banner"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
